# Observe Decastave lasting past its old 100 + 10 x level rounds, for bd inc-m790r.
# Run through tools/check_decastave_persistent.sh (fixture orc-mage-seed4-opt0822, raised to mage level 3).
@while "more --" SPACE
w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*2          # Free Advancement is the 3rd switch: the level-ups below.
SPACE
DOWN*2          # Always Rest Safely is the 5th: the dungeon refuses a rest otherwise.
SPACE
DOWN            # Ignore Spell Failure is the 6th.
SPACE
DOWN*5          # Freeze Monsters is the 11th: nothing walks in and interrupts the waiting.
SPACE
ESC
# Decastave is a level 2 spell, learnable from caster level 3, and the fixture is a level 1 mage that
# does not know it. [Ars Bellicus] holds Decastave: the Learn Spells table offers it from the pack.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*7
@until "Spellbook [Ars Bellicus]" DOWN
DOWN            # the browser highlights its middle row: one more DOWN selects the book
ENTER
@dump:book-acquired
s               # stow the book from the In-the-Air slot
@dump:book-stowed
ESC
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "You feel" ESC
@while "more --" SPACE
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "You feel" ESC
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:sheet-level
L
TAB             # the table has one page per spell level: page 2 holds the level 2 spells
DOWN*4 SPACE    # Decastave is the 5th row
@dump:learn-marked
ENTER           # open the summary box
ENTER           # confirm the box
ESC
@until "HP:" ESC
z               # "Learn at rest": the rest memorizes Decastave
@while "Confirm rest in dungeon" y
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:before-cast
m
@choose "Decastave"
@dump:after-cast
# The cast opened the inventory manager and put the staff in the In-the-Air slot, where closing the
# manager drops it (Character::GainItem, src/Annot.cpp). Swap it into the Weapon Hand, drop the dagger.
b SPACE
d
@dump:staff-wielded
ESC
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:mana-after-cast
# Each s is 1500 ticks (25 units of 60 ticks). Six of them, 9000 ticks, outlast the old EF_DLONG:
# 100 + 10 x level 3 = 130 rounds = 65 units = 3900 ticks. No rest.
s*6
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:mana-after-wait
i
@dump:inventory-after-wait
ESC
# A second casting while the staff is held.
m
@choose "Decastave"
@dump:second-cast
# A refusal opens no menu. The old build made a second staff and opened the inventory manager.
@while "'In the Air'" ESC
# Always Rest Safely rests instantly and passes no day (Player.cpp, REST_INSTANT). Switch it off: a real
# rest takes eight hours, passes the day, and Map::DaysPassed removes every Duration == -2 stati. The
# Entry Chamber refuses a real rest until the character has been to depth 4 (lib/dungeon.irh EV_REST).
w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*4
SPACE
ESC
w
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"4" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
z
@while "Confirm rest in dungeon" y
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:mana-after-rest
i
@dump:inventory-after-rest
ESC
@quit
